CLASS com/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1375 com/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLRemoteConnection
	COMMENT [bootstrap] named by its own Lombok @Slf4j logger literal
	COMMENT "com.xk72.proxy.ssl.SSLRemoteConnection".
	COMMENT Charles' connection out to the real server. It wraps the socket's streams in
	COMMENT SSLRecordParserFilter streams first, so the handshake it performs is parsed as it happens,
	COMMENT and retries with successively weaker configurations from SSLSocketConfigurationGenerator
	COMMENT until one handshake succeeds.
	FIELD field_3751 LOGGER Lorg/slf4j/Logger;
	FIELD field_3753 serverCertificates [Ljava/security/cert/Certificate;
	FIELD field_3752 handshakeCompletedListener Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1369;
	FIELD field_3754 ssl Z
		COMMENT [inferred] whether this connection is actually doing TLS: true for an https protocol,
		COMMENT or for a CONNECT that SSLHttpProxyHandler decided to proxy.
	METHOD method_3768 awaitHandshakeCompleted ()Z
		COMMENT true immediately when no handshake listener was installed.
	METHOD method_3763 getServerCertificates ()[Ljava/security/cert/Certificate;
	METHOD method_3769 isSsl ()Z
	METHOD method_3765 retryWithNextConfiguration (Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/SSLSocketConfigurationGenerator;Lcom/xk72/proxy/ProxyEvent;Lcom/xk72/proxy/ssl/class_1397;Ljava/io/IOException;)V
		COMMENT [inferred] records the failed configuration, drops the socket and reconnects so the
		COMMENT next configuration gets a fresh connection. An unrecognized_name alert is rethrown
		COMMENT instead, since retrying cannot help.
